  "release_evidence": {
    "manifest_reconstructed": true,
    "reason": "The Release workflow manifest captured partial registry state before reconciliation: npm's registry propagation lag caused seven native/wasm dependency packages' post-publish verification to time out, and the facade's first recovery attempt hit the same lag on its own verification window. Reconcile Release intentionally emits no replacement manifest, so final immutable registry metadata, successful clean-install jobs, and the annotated Git tag were combined with the preserved original manifest and inventory.",
    "known_discrepancy": "The pypi:redact-secret file hashes below are the actually-published bytes, independently verified by downloading each wheel from files.pythonhosted.org and hashing it locally, then confirmed against PyPI's JSON API. release.yml builds Python wheels twice from the same source revision (python-wheels.yml, which publish-pypi actually uploads, and independently again inside artifact-qualification.yml, whose output originally populated this inventory's Python entries), and this release's two builds were not byte-reproducible (1-5 bytes off per file; the sdist, with no compiled step, matched exactly). The checked-in artifact-inventory.json's eight wheel entries were corrected post-hoc to these true published values so the durable record is accurate to what shipped; it is therefore not a byte-exact copy of the artifact-qualification.yml run's own Python wheel output. beta.4's equivalent comparison matched exactly for all nine files, so this is not a structural inevitability, and is unexplained beyond being a non-deterministic build input (most likely an embedded timestamp). See the README's dedicated section.",
    "observed_at": "2026-09-20",
